# Pairs with AllOrNothing. Removing the visibility gate lets a reader resolve
# each key of one saga against that key's own broadcast progress instead of
# against the single registry decision, which is the split-view read the
# all-or-nothing property exists to forbid.
MODULE: AllOrNothingUngatedProjection
TARGET: AllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: drops the visibility gate so a reader sees each key at its own broadcast progress

--- FIND
ObservedPrepared(t, k) ==
    IF pend[t][k] = "pending"
    THEN IF SurfaceViaGate(t, k) THEN TRUE ELSE ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
    ELSE ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: reads go straight to the leaf's own materialised projection with
\* no gate. Mid-broadcast, one participant has applied its terminal and another
\* has not, so a snapshot read of the same saga returns a split view.
ObservedPrepared(t, k) == ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
--- END
